From ea0ecf2d8280749b50ff35d5be95daa3f8a45743 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: soulexit <metehan.tanriverdi01@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 23:49:27 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 46/54] panvk/v7: per-draw base for bindless texture and
 sampler tables

The direct (bindless) tables pointed at a device-constant base 64 GiB
below the null BO, and shaders index set memory from it with a 32-bit
index. kbase maps GPU memory at its CPU address (SAME_VA), and in
Wine/FEX processes descriptor pools land more than 64 GiB away; sets
below the base got index 0 and the GPU faulted (DXVK 2.7, which keeps
its samplers in an update-after-bind heap: black window, device lost).

The base is now the lowest of the null BO's dummy sampler and the bound
sets, computed per draw/dispatch from what is bound, so the shared
sysvals and each stage's tables agree; tables built with another base
are rebuilt. PANVK_VA_HOLE_GB=n reserves address space after device
creation to reproduce the placement in tests. PANDECODE_* keys are
accepted in panvk_env.txt.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
